NEARS-1806 re-QA (fix-cycle 2) — BUG 5: `unexamined=N` is NOT an upper bound on what the harvest skipped.
Tip 534d9093. Hermetic (no device, no app). All output verbatim.

CAUSE (base-descent-check.sh, both jq blocks — harvest ~L456-463 and unexamined ~L482-489):
    | select(($p[-1] | type) == "string")
`paths(scalars)` gives an ARRAY element a NUMERIC last path component, so every SHA that is an
array ELEMENT is filtered out of BOTH the harvest AND the unexamined tally. It is therefore
skipped and NOT counted as skipped. Pre-existing since db5328d8; what 534d9093 added is the
"UPPER BOUND" claim that is false because of it.

